# .publishing_protocol — per-repo publishing config, read by nao-aur-publish
# and by agents before any release work. Generic rules: PUBLISHING_PROTOCOL.md
# in the nao-aur-publish repo.
PUBLISH_BRANCH=supermaster
PKGBUILD_PATH=aur/PKGBUILD
AUR_PACKAGE=freeclaw
VERSION_FILE=package.json
# NOTES:
# - supermaster ONLY. master is a stale fork branch; main is upstream
#   OpenClaw — ignore both entirely.
# - package.json version must align with pkgver (e.g. 9.0.0 <-> 9).
# - AUR is published ONLY via: nao-aur-publish freeclaw vN
#   Never push this repo's git history to AUR.
# - .SRCINFO is never committed here — generated at publish time.

# POST-PUBLISH GATEWAY VERIFICATION — do on EVERY FreeClaw upgrade
# (added 2026-09-24, after v17: two live-service config bugs were found
#  only because Manu checked `openclaw --version` directly. Use the git tag
#  and `openclaw --version` — NEVER trust ~/.fe/manifest.yaml's `freeclaw:`
#  line, which was stale since v17):
#   1. Version source of truth = `openclaw --version` (and the vN git tag).
#      ~/.fe/manifest.yaml is NOT authoritative for the running version.
#   2. Gateway token in service file → regenerate the unit so the token is
#      NOT embedded: `openclaw gateway install --force` (then restart).
#      If the systemd unit hardcodes the token, re-stage with --force.
#   3. Node must run from a STABLE path, not nvm. A Node upgrade (or PATH
#      change) can strand the gateway at boot. Prefer system Node or an
#      absolute pinned path; verify `which node` before a restart.
#   Checklist before restarts/after upgrade:
#     openclaw --version
#     systemctl --user cat <gateway-service> | grep -i token   # want NOTHING
#     which node && node --version                             # want stable path
